       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the labeled maximum daily dose for adults, which is 10 mg once daily. The 70 kg weight and normal kidney and liver function don't change that limit. A dose this high risks severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock.\n\nPlease check whether 50 mg was a typo. Here are some options:\n- **Amlodipine 5 mg PO once daily.** This is the usual starting dose.\n- **Amlodipine 10 mg PO once daily.** This is the maximum dose.\n- **A different regimen.** If the patient needs more blood pressure control than 10 mg gives, adding another agent is the usual approach. Examples are an ACE inhibitor, an ARB, or a thiazide diuretic.\n\nTell me the dose you want, and I'll enter it right away."
